Built and delivered.

## What I built

**Concept — the bench dossier.** The page is the drawing set and timing record that ships with the movement: a dark bench ground with paper plates laid on it, a left index gutter and hairline running the whole route, and colour sampled from the reference photography (steel, brass, ruby jewel, blued screw). Type is Zodiak / Switzer (Fontshare) with IBM Plex Mono carrying every measured number, self-hosted in `public/fonts`.

**Sections, in order:** hero → power path → architecture → specification (paper) → workshop → finishes → reservation (paper) → footer.

**Signature component — the power path.** Six stages down a rail, with a charge line driven by one scroll progress value at 66% of the viewport; each node arms as the energy reaches it. Every stage carries a right-hand figure: a photograph where one exists, otherwise a drawn diagram of its own fact — the 72-hour scale with the refused 8% hatched, the 1 : 4,608 ratio, the ±deviation band, and a beat indicator that runs at the caliber's real five releases per second, only while that stage is on screen.

**Second peak — the architecture elevation.** Four plates drawn at true relative thickness (they sum to the 3.8mm in the spec), selectable by hover, click and keyboard, with a dimension line across the stack.

**Media.** Six CC-licensed photographs from Wikimedia Commons of comparable movements and of watchmaking work, credited in place and in the footer, each labelled a *reference plate* with an explicit statement that they are not photographs of Caliber 08 — rather than fabricating the product in CSS. I re-cropped the components photograph to remove an unrelated brand mark that appeared in the first render.

All required content is preserved, including the confirmation naming the chosen finish, its price and delivery date, and the non-binding statement in both the docket and the confirmation.

**Verified:** `npm run build` succeeds; `dreative finalize --codex --profile recommended --visual-smoke-url http://localhost:4173/` prints `DREATIVE_CHECKS_PASSED`. Inspected rendered full pages at 1440, 390 and 320 (no horizontal overflow, no console errors), plus mid-scroll power path, stack hover and keyboard selection, finish selection, form submit, and reduced motion. Two corrections came out of that pass: diagrams moved into the media column (three stages had a dead right half) and the confirmation docket no longer overlaps the paragraph above it or duplicate the aside — the aside now develops into "what happens next". Nothing was committed; the run directory is ignored by the parent repo.

Implementation complete; human taste verdict: awaiting user review. Please look at the rendered desktop and 390px views and the power-path scroll before calling it finished.